{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): g'day. i'll grab your obs. blood pressure's one twenty eight over eighty two, pulse seventy six. and the list here has lexapro, twenty milligrams.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): nah, that's off. the chemist box is ten milligrams. she's only on ten.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (PATIENT): ten.",
  "[SEG0004] person_1 (NURSE): right, i'll flag it. my sister's on lexapro too, ever since her bub arrived, and they still can't settle her dose. not your drama. in you go.",
  "[SEG0005] person_4 (DOCTOR): come through, have a seat. what's been going on?",
  "[SEG0006] person_3 (PATIENT): cramps.",
  "[SEG0007] person_4 (DOCTOR): cramps, yeah. where do you get them, and how long's that been?",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (PATIENT): tummy. year.",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): lower tummy, mostly. and she bloats right up after lunch.",
  "[SEG0010] person_4 (DOCTOR): bloating as well. does anything ease the cramp when it hits?",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (PATIENT): pooing.",
  "[SEG0012] person_4 (DOCTOR): so it settles once you've been to the loo. and the stools, hard, loose, or a bit of both?",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (PATIENT): both.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): she flips. some weeks she can't go, then it's loose for days. whole year's been like that.",
  "[SEG0015] person_4 (DOCTOR): any blood you've noticed, in the bowl or on the paper?",
  "[SEG0016] person_3 (PATIENT): no.",
  "[SEG0017] person_4 (DOCTOR): and weight, have you dropped any?",
  "[SEG0018] person_3 (PATIENT): no.",
  "[SEG0019] person_4 (DOCTOR): what about fevers? been hot or shivery at all?",
  "[SEG0020] person_3 (PATIENT): umm. sort of. not really.",
  "[SEG0021] person_4 (DOCTOR): bit muddy, that. we'll leave it. how's work treating you?",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (PATIENT): stressful.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): she's a project manager. deadlines every week. skips lunch most days.",
  "[SEG0024] person_4 (DOCTOR): that kind of pressure can wind the gut right up. the bowel's got its own nerves, and when you're stressed they fire off and the muscle clamps down in spasms. that's often what the cramp actually is.",
  "[SEG0025] person_4 (DOCTOR): mind if i have a feel of your tummy?",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (PATIENT): yeah.",
  "[SEG0027] person_4 (DOCTOR): soft. a little tender low on the left. no lumps.",
  "[SEG0028] person_4 (DOCTOR): are you taking anything for the bowels? fibre, a laxative?",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (PATIENT): metamucil.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): hit and miss. maybe three days a week. she forgets.",
  "[SEG0031] person_4 (DOCTOR): any allergies to medicines?",
  "[SEG0032] person_3 (PATIENT): no.",
  "[SEG0033] person_4 (DOCTOR): okay. i'd like some bloods today. full blood count, a coeliac screen, and err inflammatory markers. we'll book them before you head off.",
  "[SEG0034] person_4 (DOCTOR): food wise, smaller meals, ease off the coffee if you can, and try the metamucil every day instead of now and then. a warm wheat bag on the tummy helps when it clamps.",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (FAMILY_MEMBER): when do we come back?",
  "[SEG0036] person_4 (DOCTOR): about six weeks, once the bloods are in. reception can book that on the way out."
 ],
